Read Receipts — licensing
=========================

This repository is licensed in two parts, because it contains two different
kinds of work.

  1. THE CODE is under the MIT licence, reproduced in full below. Take it,
     learn from it, ship it in your own project. That is the point.

  2. THE GAME — the case scripts, the artwork and the audio — is NOT under the
     MIT licence. It is proprietary. See the CONTENT-LICENSE file in this same
     directory.

WHAT COUNTS AS CODE
-------------------

The MIT grant below covers every file in this repository EXCEPT:

  - content/cases/**      the sixteen case packs, in every language
  - assets/**             artwork, cover images, audio
  - docs/storybook.md     and docs/storybook.html — the case scripts in prose

Those are covered by CONTENT-LICENSE.

Everything else is MIT: src/, app/, supabase/, tools/, the tests, the config,
the other docs. That includes the deduction engine in src/engine/, which is the
part most worth reading.

WHY THE SPLIT
-------------

The engine is a piece of software design and it is more useful shared. The
cases are the product — roughly twenty thousand words that took months, and
twelve of the sixteen are what a player pays for. A single MIT licence over
both granted the world the right to sell the game, which was never the
intention and was a drafting mistake rather than a decision.

Changed 2026-09-10. See docs/LEGAL-REVIEW.md, Count 1, for the full account
including what this change cannot undo.


